=head1 NAME

_ROTATE_TO_AZEL_ - Rotate image to Az-El system and display

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This primitive can be used when an image has been made in
non-Az-El coordinates, but needs to be displayed in them.
An example would be a HARP pointing gridded in tracking
coordinates.  We must process this data in the coordinate
system used for the observation such that slices
align with the (typically) 5-point pattern, but we
should display in Az-El in order to help the operator
verify the direction of the pointing offset.

The map is first enlarged using sqorst to give a reasonable
number of pixels for rotation.  The required angle is
then estimated via astRate and appled using the KAPPA
rotate task.

=head1 PARAMETERS

=over 4

=item SUFFIX = STRING (Given)

Output file name suffix.  [azel]

=back

